{
  "statement": "Trustworthiness is essential in a bookkeeping system to protect sensitive financial data and ensure user accountability. Requirement TRU-01 mandates encryption for data protection during transmission and storage, while TRU-02 establishes role-based access control to restrict permissions. TRU-03 ensures an immutable audit trail for accountability, and TRU-04 validates data input to prevent unauthorized entries. TRU-05 supports two-factor authentication for enhanced security, and TRU-06 logs user access for transparency. Lastly, TRU-07 ensures users can only access relevant data, maintaining privacy and integrity.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["SAF-04", "EFF-07"],
      "type": "logical",
      "description": "The requirement for an immutable audit trail (TRU-03) may conflict with the need for thorough error correction and timely logging of transactions (EFF-07), potentially hindering performance during high transaction volumes."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["SAF-02", "RES-05"],
      "type": "resource",
      "description": "The strict adherence to double-entry principles (SAF-02) may limit flexibility in complying with varying local and international accounting standards (RES-05), impacting the system's adaptability."
    }
  ],
